<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE topic PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Topic//EN" "topic.dtd">
<topic id="git-addon-push-pull-with-merge-or-rebase">
  <title>Push and Pull Changes</title>
  
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <indexterm>Git Client add-on<indexterm>push</indexterm></indexterm>
        <indexterm>Git Client add-on<indexterm>pull</indexterm></indexterm>
        <indexterm>Git Client add-on<indexterm>merge</indexterm></indexterm>
        <indexterm>Git Client add-on<indexterm>rebase</indexterm></indexterm>
      </keywords>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
  <body>
    <p id="p_mhy_w4y_kpb">After you commit changes to your local repository, use <xref
        href="git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts.dita#git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts/action_push"><uicontrol><image
            href="../img/PreviousReference16.png"/>Push</uicontrol></xref> to make them available in
      the remote repository.</p>
    <p id="p_nhy_w4y_kpb">Use <xref
        href="git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts.dita#git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts/action_pull"><uicontrol>Pull</uicontrol></xref>
      when you need to bring other people's commits from the remote repository into your local
      repository.</p>
    <p id="p_gj1_cl5_1dc">In the <uicontrol>Pull</uicontrol> drop-down menu, you can choose
      between <xref
        href="git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts.dita#git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts/action_pull_merge"><uicontrol>Pull
          (merge)</uicontrol></xref> and <xref
        href="git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts.dita#git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts/action_pull_rebase"><uicontrol>Pull
          (rebase)</uicontrol></xref>. The action you use becomes the default action of the toolbar
      button.</p>
    <p>Use <xref
        href="git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts.dita#git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts/action_pull_other_branch"><uicontrol>Pull...</uicontrol></xref>
      when you need to pull from a remote branch other than the tracked branch.</p>
    <note id="note_jnw_bpy_kpb">When you push a local branch that does not have a corresponding
      remote branch, a remote branch with the same name is created automatically.</note>
  </body>
</topic>